<title>HONG KONG: Swire JV clinches HK waste contract.</title>
<headline>Swire JV clinches HK waste contract.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong's Environmental Protection Department has awarded a contract to a Swire Pacific Ltd joint venture for waste transfer facilities for the territory's outlying islands, the government said on Monday.</p>
<p>The contract was awarded to Swire BFI Waste Services Ltd, a company co-owned by American waste management company Browning Ferris Industries Inc, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Swire BFI will design, construct and operate the facilities for 15 years. Capital cost of the project is about HK$324 million and the annual operation cost around HK$45 million.</p>
<p>--Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
